export anchor FilmReelStyle:
    number: 357
    screen: VideoEditor
    name: Film reel
    idea: An editing bench of real film, where every track is a strip of amber celluloid with sprocket holes, audio runs as an optical soundtrack, media sits in labelled film cans and grease pencil marks the selection and the marker.
    base: dark
    palette:
        bench: #120c08, page, rack ground and the style sheet
        darkroom: #0d0805, header, rack well and sprocket hole shade
        cueCard: #1d140d, the cue card and swatch cells
        celluloid: #3b2612, film strip base and the gate
        frame: #5a3a1a, picture clips as frames on the strip
        labelTape: #eadcc0, can labels, the header tape and play
        ink: #ecdfca, text
        muted: #b29f86, small typewritten asides
        amber: #f2b25c, section titles, timecode, track ids, Export and focus
        edgeCode: #ffd08c, clip names printed on the strip
        greasePencil: #ffb39e, selection loop, marker cross and handwritten notes
    type:
        Labels and data use a typewriter stack, American Typewriter, Courier
        Prime, Courier New. Section titles use a hand stack, Bradley Hand,
        Segoe Print, Chalkboard SE, Comic Neue, at 22px in amber. Body is
        system sans 14px. The timecode is typewriter 20px bold in amber, the
        picture card typewriter up to 32px, edge codes typewriter 11px bold,
        notes in the hand stack.
    layout:
        The header shows a strip of cream label tape, slightly tilted, split
        by dashed tears into Brightwork Cut, Launch teaser, 1080p and 24
        fps. On the right a tiny film strip of 16 empty frames reads 0%
        rendered and no frames yet, then an amber pill Export with a reel
        icon and a solid lip. The bench is a grid. The Gate takes the left
        with the viewer framed by celluloid and round sprocket holes down
        both sides, then amber timecode, round transport buttons with a
        cream play, and reel length with the duration. The Cue card on the
        right lists Position 960 by 540, Scale 100 percent, Opacity 100
        percent and Cross dissolve 12 frames in typewriter rows with dashed
        rules, and a handwritten note. Cans fill a full row, five round film
        cans with cream tape labels giving name, duration and picture or
        sound. The Splice rack shows each track as an amber film strip with
        sprocket holes along both edges, picture clips as frames divided by
        dark frame lines with a light edge, audio clips with an optical
        soundtrack wave and the name printed as edge code. The selected
        title frame has a dashed grease pencil loop, a cross and the
        handwritten word selected. A grease pencil cross and dashed line
        mark cut to logo, and a cream playhead with a down triangle reads 18
        s. At phone width the cans and cue card hide and track labels reduce
        to ids.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between bench areas, 8px between strips.
    density: Medium. Gate, cue card, five cans and four strips.
    corners: Round cans and transport buttons, 22px pill Export, 2px to 6px on strips and cards.
    borders: Frame lines are 2px dark bars with a 2px #c08a4a edge along each frame, the cue card has dashed rules, tape has dashed tears.
    shadows: Heavy drop shadows under cans and the gate, a 3px solid lip under Export.
    icons: Filled transport glyphs, a reel on Export, a cross for selected and for the marker. Film cans and sprocket holes are drawn with gradients.
    focus: A 3px amber outline offset 3px.
    tone: Workshop talk, such as Cans, Splice rack, reel length and no frames yet.
